    "description": "As Lead Developer at X-CellSystem I was responsible for creating desktop applications, services and web applications for clients.\n\nMy most recent task was designing an application to allow our client to submit reports and documentation to the CBER division of the FDA.\n\nI replaced a system where documents were prepared and filed by hand via USB Drives sent via Fedex with an automated system to submit documents through the FDA Gateway.\n\nA desktop application was created for managing the documents and responses via the clients laptop.  Windows Services were created to parse the documents for reliability and accuracy then reformatted into the very specific folder and document names required by the FDA.\n\nAn AS2 server was hosted on Amazon EC2 using the specific configuration and encryption keys required\nby the FDA to allow communication.  The Windows Service was additionally used to properly compress and encrypt the submissions to FDA specifications.\n\nOther projects I was responsible for included a prototype fingerprint ID system and a data collection application to consolidate Blood Center information from the FDA to a database searchable with Google Maps.",
